s BCL2L11"], "releaseDate": "2026-03-25", "speciesName": "Mus musculus", "inferredFrom": [139918], "species": [{"dbId": 48892, "displayName": "Mus musculus", "name": ["Mus musculus", "M. musculus", "Mm", "house mouse"], "taxId": "10090", "abbreviation": "MMU", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "transition", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}], "revised": [{"dbId": 3145024, "displayName": "Orlic-Milacic, M, 2013-02-13", "dateTime": "2013-02-14 00:17:45", "className": "InstanceEdit", "schemaClass": "InstanceEdit"}], "species": [48887], "summation": [{"dbId": 179063, "displayName": "MAPK8 (JNK) phosphorylates BCL2L11 (BIM) on a DLC-binding mo...", "text": "MAPK8 (JNK) phosphorylates BCL2L11 (BIM) on a DLC-binding motif (DKSTQTP), involved in dynein (DYNLL2 i.e. DLC1) binding and sequestration of BCL2L11 (BIM) to the cytoskeleton. Phosphorylated BCL2L11 dissociates from dynein. Three sites in BCL2L11 match the JNK consensus: S44, T56 and S58 in BCL2L11 isoform BimL (these residues correspond to S104, T116 and S118 in BCL2L11 isoform BimEL), and all sites appear to be phosphorylated by MAPK8 (JNK) both in vitro and in vivo (Lei and Davis 2003). ", "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "updateTrackers": [{"dbId": 9787891, "displayName": "Update Tracker - [Reaction:139918] Phosphorylation of BIM by JNK - v44:[add_removeOutput, modifyText]", "action": ["add_removeOutput", "modifyText"], "updatedInstance": [139918], "className": "UpdateTracker", "schemaClass": "UpdateTracker"}, {"dbId": 9779109, "displayName": "Update Tracker - [Reaction:139918] Phosphorylation of BIM by JNK - v66:[addInput, addOutput]", "action": ["addInput", "addOutput"], "updatedInstance": [139918], "className": "UpdateTracker", "schemaClass": "UpdateTracker"}